    "legend": { "x": -700, "y": 0, "w": 560, "color": "green", "text": "How a block reads on the calendar\n\nReserved (solid green) — approved. The team name is visible to everyone.\n\nPending (amber, dashed) — requested but not decided. The slot is already held, so no other team can take it.\n\nClosed (hatched) — outside that day's hours, or a closure date.\n\nEvery screen assumes one facility with one bookable space." },
    "flow": { "x": -700, "y": 1220, "w": 560, "color": "gray", "text": "The loop\n\nCoach picks an open slot → picks a length (30 / 60 / 90 min) → submits.\n\nThe request lands in the approver's inbox AND in the Approvals queue. Both do the same thing; whoever gets there first decides it.\n\nApprove → block turns green with the team name. Decline → approver types a reason, coach sees it in email and in My requests." }
  }
